Subject: vmm emit the scoped private GPU report before guest execution
Why: AC-T7.4.1: the VM process emits its scoped private GPU report before the guest runs, arms the managed lifeline before native initialization, awaits an existing input owner before device initialization, carries only explicit managed pipes across its final Unix exec and adopts the report writer without helper inheritance on Windows: the protocol the node's vendored API (vendor/shards) speaks. Shards commits 1ab4a163, bbe0e8fd, 93687a2c, 10f66c5c, 1108260c and b128aaa5.

